    {
      "id": "po1lxyn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO INFRASTRUCTURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Infrastructure is broadly classified into Economic Infrastructure and Social Infrastructure.",
        "Economic infrastructure directly supports economic activities through transport, communication, power, banking, and irrigation.",
        "Social infrastructure indirectly aids economic growth by enhancing human capital through education, health, housing, and sanitation.",
        "Adequate infrastructure is essential for lowering production costs, increasing trade efficiency, and driving national development.",
        "Government initiatives actively address major infrastructural bottlenecks such as funding gaps, execution delays, and regional imbalances."
      ],
      "id": "bzku315"
    },
